  "body": "## What happens\n\nPR #4482 (#4340) disables Duplicate in the tool editor while the main form draft has unapplied changes. The independent pre-review of head `6189d81` found that three other drafts in the editor are not part of that check, and a Duplicate still drops them without a word:\n\n- the holder draft (`editor.holder`, `ToolProfileUi`; it has its own \"Apply holder\": custom outline, library pick, gauge length, projection);\n- the body draft (`editor.body`, `ToolBodyUi`; \"Apply body\": imported mesh, axis, offset, pieces). An unapplied body import is the worst case;\n- the stack draft (`view.stack`, `StackDraft.links`; keyed by tool name, so it resets for the copy).\n\n`open_tool_in_library` builds a fresh editor for the copy with default holder and body drafts. The disabled hover text \"the draft has unapplied changes\" reads as if the guard covers everything.\n\n## Expected\n\nDuplicate is disabled, with the reason, while any of the four drafts (form, holder, body, stack) has unapplied changes. The hover text names which draft.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A test for each draft: an unapplied change disables Duplicate, a click queues nothing, the draft is kept; after its Apply (or Cancel), Duplicate is enabled.\n- No change to toolpaths, posts or the project file.\n\nAfter #4482 merges.\n",
